ALVA — Major CPU Intelligence Update: Human Behavior, Difficulty Rebalancing & Advanced Strategic Awareness

Your mission

Work directly in the GitHub repository hiyroscript/alva.

I want a major, carefully engineered update to CPU Intelligence.

This is one of the most important gameplay updates for Alva. Quality, stability, believable behavior, and preservation of existing systems are more important than speed of implementation.

The current CPU Intelligence is an excellent foundation. I love the new intelligence system, its understanding of combat, its ability to use different fighters, and its existing decision-making. Do not replace, dismantle, or significantly simplify it. Build on what already exists.

However, there are two major problems:

1. CPUs are currently too strong, especially on Easy. Even Easy can feel excessively efficient and difficult to beat.
2. CPUs need substantially more strategic intelligence and human-like behavior. They should understand the entire match, make meaningful long-term decisions, use stages intelligently, recognize when to fight versus when to protect themselves, and adapt their playstyle to their actual situation.

The most important requirement is:

CPUs must feel like real human players of different skill levels, not perfect machines, passive dummies, or scripted bots.

A CPU can be very smart without being mechanically perfect or unfairly difficult. The objective is to make CPUs smarter in their decisions, while keeping their actual execution and consistency appropriate to the selected difficulty.

