19. Final development instructions

Take this update seriously. It is a major behavioral evolution of CPU Intelligence, not a collection of quick fixes.

Avoid the tempting but incorrect solution of merely lowering Easy’s reaction speed, reducing attack frequency, or adding random delays.

The true goal is to improve how the CPU understands Alva and how naturally it makes decisions.

Keep what is already excellent.

Extend what is incomplete.

Correct what feels unfair or mechanical.

Build a CPU that genuinely understands when to attack, when to defend, when to retreat, when to recover, when to wait, when to control the stage, and when the situation demands changing its entire approach.

Above all:

I want every CPU to feel like a real person playing Alva at the selected difficulty.

Easy should feel like a casual human player.

Medium should feel like a competent human player.

Hard should feel like a highly experienced human player.

Brutal should feel like an elite human player.

Every level should have judgment, imperfections, patience, and strategic purpose.

